<title>HUNGARY: Central Europe's CESI slips as Czech shares fall.</title>
<headline>Central Europe's CESI slips as Czech shares fall.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The CESI Central European Share Index slipped on Tuesday to close at 1,514.04 points, down 3.05 points or 0.20 percent, the Budapest Stock Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>The index fell mainly because the declines of Czech shares.</p>
<p>The index, which has been published since February 1, reflects trends of 50 shares on the Budapest, Prague and Warsaw bourses.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 266 2410</p>
